window.bookSummaryJSON = "<b>In a world ruled by vampires, the deadliest weapon isn't silver or sunlight—it's hope.</b><br><br>Ana Lazarescu survived the blood-soaked halls of Umbra High, but victory came at devastating cost. With her family slaughtered and a bounty on her head, she's forced to seek refuge with the human resistance—a hidden community of survivors carving out existence in the shadows of vampire rule.<br><br>But the resistance harbors secrets darker than the night itself.<br><br>When Ana discovers the shapeshifters—humans who've weaponized vampire blood to transform into beasts of vengeance—she's drawn to Luca, a wolf shifter whose humanity slips away with each transformation. Meanwhile, her forbidden blood bond with Stefan, the vampire who helped her escape, evolves into something neither of them expected—something that could get them both killed.<br><br>As a centuries-old Victorian vampire wages psychological warfare against the camp, paranoia spreads like a virus, turning allies into enemies overnight. Ana watches the community fracture from within, forcing her to forge alliances with unlikely figures—including the former high school tormentor who once made her life hell.<br><br>With an orphaned child to protect, traitors in their midst, and a haunted past she cannot outrun, Ana must guide her fractured found family through mounting dangers while searching for the one man who might hold the key to humanity's survival—her long-lost father.<br><br>When the world thirsts for your blood, resistance becomes your legacy.<br><br><b>The Beast Within is the pulse-pounding second installment in the Blood Legacy series—a dark, immersive tale of survival, sacrifice, and the blurred lines between monster and hero. Perfect for fans of The Hunger Games, Vampire Academy, and Shadow and Bone.</b>"; 
